Every client dashboard now pulls real-time data from all four channels
(Meta, Shopify, Google Ads, TikTok) instead of just Meta — same
on-demand "pull, don't sync" pattern as the existing Meta integration:

- Shopify: Admin API client + manual store-connect flow (no OAuth app
  review needed) + live daily-metrics pull.
- Google Ads: OAuth client (API v24) + agency-wide MCC flow using the
  customer_client GAQL hierarchy query (listAccessibleCustomers only
  returns directly-granted accounts, not an MCC's client list) + live
  report/pacing pull with proactive token refresh.
- TikTok: OAuth client + manual token-paste flow (primary path, given
  ambiguity in TikTok's OAuth docs) + live report/pacing pull with
  reactive refresh-on-auth-error.
- Both Google Ads and TikTok OAuth callbacks refuse to auto-connect
  when the account list is ambiguous (0 or >1 accounts) rather than
  guessing, since a wrong guess would attribute one client's ad data
  to a different client's workspace.
- New shared getLiveAdsReport() blends Meta+Google+TikTok into one
  report for Overview and AI Copilot; channel-page.tsx calls each
  provider directly since it only ever shows one channel at a time.
- AI Copilot's insight engine now also pulls Shopify live (it was
  still reading the database table that live mode stopped populating)
  and skips ROAS-change insights for any provider whose fetch failed,
  so a failed pull can't masquerade as a real performance drop.
- Settings page has connect UI, health checks, and partial-failure
  banners for all four providers now, not just Meta.

Documented, honest scope gaps: Shopify sessions (no ShopifyQL Plus),
Google Ads reach/funnel fields, TikTok revenue/funnel fields, and
Quality-Score-style rankings for Google Ads/TikTok are all 0/absent
without deeper API access this pass — same as Meta's existing gaps.

tsc, lint, tests (11/11), and production build all pass clean.

